earch assistant, a multi-agent orchestration system, or something else entirely. Walk us through the architecture, the tools and models involved, and how information flows through the system. Then discuss the tradeoffs you have made in building or configuring it: where did you prioritize autonomy vs. control, cost vs. quality, latency vs. thoroughness? What failure modes have you encountered, and how do you handle them?","type":"long","value":"","isValueOther":false,"hasOther":"no","options":[]},{"id":"72","isRequired":true,"question":"You have a 7B-parameter language model with three candidate fine-tuned checkpoints, and you are not sure which one performs best in production. You also have a legacy model currently in production. You have a large user base but cannot afford to expose too many users to a potentially worse experience during evaluation.  Design a rollout and serving strategy using Thompson sampling to efficiently identify and promote the best checkpoint while minimizing negative user impact. In your response, discuss how you would define the reward signal, how you would structure the bandit arms (including the legacy model), how the posterior updates work, what serving infrastructure is required to route traffic dynamically, and what safeguards you would put in place (e.g., minimum traffic to legacy, early stopping criteria). Address practical considerations such as cold-start, non-stationarity, and how you would decide when the experiment is conclusive.","type":"long","value":"","isValueOther":false,"hasOther":"no","options":[]},{"id":"73","isRequired":true,"question":"Will you now or in the future require employer sponsorship for work authorization in the United States (including CPT, OPT, H-1B, or other employment-based visa sponsorship)?","type":"long","value":"","isValueOther":false,"hasOther":"no","options":[]}],"genderId":[],"ethnicityId":[],"veteranStatusId":[],"disabilityId":[]}}}